          "text": "The user asks two things:\n1. Why did I say \"по плану их место — anonymous namespace\"?\n2. Why then does `rm_crlf_symbols` have external linkage? (i.e., it's a global function too, so why single out the new ones?)\n\nI should answer: \n- Anonymous namespace = internal linkage, so the name is visible only in this TU. It's the modern C++ replacement for `static` at namespace scope. Purpose: avoid name collisions and signal \"this is a local helper, not part of the interface.\"\n- Consistency argument: `rm_crlf_symbols` and `file_to_bytes_string` are also free functions at global scope with external linkage. So my recommendation wasn't consistent with the existing file style. Two options: (a) wrap ALL helpers in anonymous namespace (or mark static), (b) leave as-is following existing style.\n\nSo the honest answer: it was my preference/plan, not a defect. And `rm_crlf_symbols` indeed has external linkage — same situation. So if we care, we should be consistent: either all helpers in anon namespace, or none.\n\nDoes it matter practically? For an exe with a single TU, no. It matters when:\n- multiple TUs linked together and same-named helpers collide → ODR/link error.\n- header-provided helpers.\n- It's a signal of intent.\n\nAlso note: it's not a compiler error; it's about hygiene. And `main` must have external linkage (that's the entry point) — don't put main in anon namespace.\n\nAlso mention: `check.exe` currently is one TU (check.cpp only)? Let me verify: tests/CMakeLists add_executable(check check.cpp) — yes single source. So no collision risk now. But if check.cpp grows / combines TUs, matter.\n\nLet me also note the real reason my \"plan\" said anon namespace: it's the idiomatic C++ way, and §4.3 idiom. But since the file already has global helpers, consistency should win: apply uniformly or not at all (§5 п.2 единый стиль).\n\nAlso clarify `const inline` variable got external linkage; functions at namespace scope are external by default (unless static/anon). So all these helpers are externally visible.\n\nRecommendation: simplest consistent approach — wrap all file-local helpers (file_to_bytes_string, rm_crlf_symbols, escape_window, print_header) in one anonymous namespace, keep main outside. Or mark none. I lean wrap, since it's cheap and documents intent. But it's optional.\n\nKeep concise. No edits (plan mode).\n\nLet me write.",
