lid UTF-8 run → dropped, and the spaces in \"N \" and \" . \" and \": \" are the original ASCII spaces). Actually \"N    . : abd\": N, space, [4 spaces where \"должно быть целым числом\" was], \".\", space, \":\", space, \"abd\". Hmm \"Получено\" also became blank but there's no space shown? \"N    . : abd\" — between \":\" and \"abd\" there's one space (original). \"Получено\" (8 chars) → dropped entirely? \n\nThe point: invalid UTF-8 byte sequences get replaced by nothing (or the console drops them), leaving only ASCII. That matches \"empty symbols\".\n\nActually a cleaner explanation of the blank: when CTest converts its internal buffer to UTF-16 for WriteConsoleW using CP_UTF8, invalid sequences map to U+FFFD (replacement). But then the console font... no. Or CTest/CMake might *strip* invalid bytes when building its output string earlier. Either way: the CP1251 bytes are gone because the sink is UTF-8. [ПРЕДПОЛОЖЕНИЕ, СРЕДНИЙ] on exact replacement-vs-drop.\n\nBut the more important, certain point: the compile option can't affect file bytes.\n\nNow let me also address her current lean: she's now between `-Q -O file` and `>0x7F → \\xNN`. She said \"это было сделано после некоторых рассуждений\" — she wants commentary on the *experiment*, then presumably we'll finalize.\n\nLet me structure the answer:\n\n1. What `/utf-8` actually is (two sub-flags).\n2. Step 1 (`/utf-8`): why warnings — source assumed UTF-8 but files are CP1251; C4828; literals mis-decoded. Note C4828 is a warning, so \"link error\" is likely mislabeled — [ПРЕДПОЛОЖЕНИЕ].\n3. Step 2 (`/source-charset:cp1251`): why \"не работало\" — \"cp1251\" likely not a recognized name; MSVC wants \"windows-1251\" / numeric / \"iso-8859-1\" / \"utf-8\". [ПРЕДПОЛОЖЕНИЕ, СРЕДНИЙ — verify docs].\n4. Step 3 (`/source-charset:windows-1251 /execution-charset:utf-8`): this IS correct for literals (no warnings, correct UTF-8 literals). But it can't fix the needle — needle is **file bytes**, not a literal. So the \"N    .