d::expected=12, from_chars<double>=11. So \"2-3 below 15\" = 12-13, but std::print forces 14. So correct her.\n\nActually, let me double check std::print GCC version. libstdc++ `<print>`: added in GCC 14. Yes. And MSVC: `<print>` in VS 2022 17.4+. And C++23 `std::println` too GCC 14.\n\nSo minimum GCC 14. Confirm.\n\nAlso she might be running with `-std=c++23`? Her CMake sets CMAKE_CXX_STANDARD 23. GCC 15 defaults? Fine.\n\nLet me write the answer concisely, numbered to match her points.\n\nI'll mark [ФАКТ/МНЕНИЕ/ПРЕДПОЛОЖЕНИЕ] + confidence.\n\nAlso note the distinction \"зафиксировать версии\" (reproducibility, §5 layer 15 item 9) vs \"минималка\" (support floor). She's conflating; clarify.\n\nLet me write.",
