          "text": "Let me review the two sections.\n\n**Section \"Минимальные версии инструментов\" (lines 77-80)** — currently empty (just Windows/Linux headers). She asks how to figure out the minimum versions herself.\n\n**Section \"Известные ограничения проекта\" (lines 177-195)** — has 5 bullets. Let me verify each for accuracy.\n\nBullet 1 (chcp 1251): \"под windows для корректного вывода кириллицы в консоль команда chcp 1251\". This is accurate for *direct exe run* in cmd, but we just established that for *ctest --output-on-failure* chcp does NOT help (CMake WriteConsoleW UTF-8). So this bullet is now INCOMPLETE/partially wrong: it says \"for correct Cyrillic output in console use chcp 1251\" — but that's only true for direct program runs, not for ctest echo. Given the whole recent saga, this bullet needs a caveat. Also, the check diagnostic now uses \\xNN (ASCII-safe), so check output is readable regardless. So the bullet is inaccurate in light of what we just learned. Should flag.\n\nActually wait — is chcp 1251 accurate at all now? For direct exe run in cmd at cp866, chcp 1251 makes it readable (she confirmed \"даёт нормальный 'Строка 1...'\"). So for direct runs it's correct. For ctest echo it doesn't help. So the bullet should be split or caveated. Flag this.\n\nBullet 2 (невалидные кириллические символы на linux + iconv): accurate. The iconv note: \"без -o будет вывод в консоль текста в корректной кодировке\" — actually `iconv -f cp1251 -t utf8 input_file` without -o writes to stdout, which in a UTF-8 terminal displays correctly. Fine. One nit: earlier journal noted iconv adds a trailing newline issue if no trailing \\n — \"при iconv -f cp1251 -t utf8 input_file ps1 сразу после последнего символа появляется\" (some quirk). Not sure. Could mention but minor. Actually the journal 09-23 \"не забывать исправить. при iconv ... сразу после последнего символа появляется. т.к. нет \\n в конце - надо добавить.\" So there's a known caveat about trailing newline. 